	<div id="main"><h1>Governor's Executive Orders 2006</h1>
<div id="navcontainer">
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_001">Executive Order 06-01</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Jan. 10)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_002">Executive Order 06-02</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt extends the deadline for the State Retirement Consolidation Commission to issue a final report and terminate operations to March 1, 2006. (Jan. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_003">Executive Order 06-03</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Missouri Healthcare Information Technology Task Force. (Jan. 17)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_027">Executive Order 09-27</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_004">Executive Order 06-04</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt transfers functions, personnel, property, etc. of the Division of Finance, the State Banking Board, the Division of Credit Unions, and the Division of Professional Registration to the Department of Insurance, effective August 28, 2006. The Department of Insurance is renamed the Missouri Department of Insurance, Financial Institutions and Professional Registration under the Governor's Executive Branch Reorganization Plan of 2006. (Feb. 1)<br>- Superseded and Replaced by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2019/eo2">Executive Order 19-02</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_005">Executive Order 06-05</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt transfers functions, personnel, property, etc. of the Missouri Rx Plan Advisory Commission to the Missouri Department of Social Services under the Governor's Executive Branch Reorganization Plan of 2006, effective August 28, 2006. (Feb. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_006">Executive Order 06-06</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt transfers functions, personnel, property, etc. of the Missouri Assistive Technology Advisory Council to the Missouri Department of Elementary and Secondary Education under the Governor's Executive Branch Reorganization Plan of 2006, effective August 28, 2006. Certain provisions of Executive Order 04-08 are rescinded. (Feb. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_007">Executive Order 06-07</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt transfers functions, personnel, property, etc. of the Missouri Life Sciences Research Board to the Missouri Department of Economic Development under the Governor's Executive Branch Reorganization Plan of 2006, effective August 28, 2006. (Feb. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_008">Executive Order 06-08</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt dedicates and names the state office building, located at 1616 Missouri Boulevard, Jefferson City, Missouri, in honor of George Washington Carver. (Feb. 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_009">Executive Order 06-09</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt reauthorizes the Homeland Security Advisory Council as a continuing advisory body and updates the structure of the homeland security function within the Department of Public Safety to reflect the current organization and operation. (Feb. 10)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_010">Executive Order 06-10</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Government, Faith-based and Community Partnership. (Mar. 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_011">Executive Order 06-11</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to the severe weather that began on March 11, 2006. (Mar. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_012">Executive Order 06-12</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to the severe weather that began on March 11, 2006. (Mar. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_013">Executive Order 06-13</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on March 11, 2006. (Mar. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_014">Executive Order 06-14</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began on April 2, 2006. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_015">Executive Order 06-15</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to the severe weather that began on April 2, 2006. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_016">Executive Order 06-16</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began March 29, 2006. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_017">Executive Order 06-17</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began on March 8, 2006. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_018">Executive Order 06-18</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt authorizes certified investigators from various state agencies to temporarily exercise full statewide police authority. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_019"><strong>Executive Order 06-19</strong></a><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on March 29, 2006. (Apr. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_020">Executive Order 06-20</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt acknowledges the regional state of emergency within various Missouri counties and directs interim requirements for overdimension and overweight permits for commercial motor carriers engaged in intrastate disaster relief efforts. (Apr. 5)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_021">Executive Order 06-21</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (June 2)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_022">Executive Order 06-22</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt directs the transfers of all tobacco settlement moneys to a single account, the Healthy Families Trust Fund, and rescinds <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2001/eo01_005">Executive Order 01-05</a>. (June 22)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_023">Executive Order 06-23</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt formalizes the organizational structure of the Statewide Interoperability Executive Committee and places it under the authority of the Homeland Security Advisory Council for the purpose of developing a statewide communications strategic plan. (June 27)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_024">Executive Order 06-24</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Missouri Abraham Lincoln Bicentennial Commission. (July 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_025">Executive Order 06-25</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began on July 19, 2006. (July 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_026">Executive Order 06-26</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities due to the severe weather beginning July 19, 2006. (July 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_027">Executive Order 06-27</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on July 19, 2006. (July 21)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_028">Executive Order 06-28</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Missouri Department of Transportation authority to issue emergency declarations of regional or local emergency for the limited purpose of temporarily suspending regulations to motor carriers. (July 22)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_029">Executive Order 06-29</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Missouri Department of Transportation authority to issue emergency declarations of regional or local emergency for the limited purpose of temporarily suspending regulations to motor carriers. The director is also authorized to issue overdimension and overweight permits for commercial motor carriers engaged in interstate and intrastate disaster relief. (Aug. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_030">Executive Order 06-30</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt extends the declaration of emergency contained in <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_025">Executive Order 06-25</a> and the terms of <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_027">Executive Order 06-27</a> through September 22, 2006, for clean up in the aftermath of severe storms in the east central part of the state. (Aug. 18)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_031">Executive Order 06-31</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe storms that began September 22, 2006. (Sep. 23)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_032">Executive Order 06-32</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on September 22, 2006. (Sep. 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_033">Executive Order 06-33</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders all state employees to enable any state-owned wireless telecommunications device capable of receiving text messages or e-mails to receive wireless AMBER Alerts. (Oct. 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_034">Executive Order 06-34</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt amends <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2003/eo03_026">Executive Order 03-26</a> relating to the reorganization of the Information Technology Advisory Board. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_035">Executive Order 06-35</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for Job Creation and Economic Growth. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_036">Executive Order 06-36</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for Laboratory Services and Utilization. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_037">Executive Order 06-37</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for Rural Affairs. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_038">Executive Order 06-38</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for State Employee Career Opportunity. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_039">Executive Order 06-39</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Mental Health Transformation Working Group. (Oct. 11)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_040">Executive Order 06-40</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for State Service Delivery Efficiency. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_041">Executive Order 06-41</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt establishes the Interdepartmental Coordination Council for Water Quality. (Oct. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_042">Executive Order 06-42</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Oct. 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_043">Executive Order 06-43</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders state offices to be closed on Friday, November 24, 2006. (Oct. 24)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_044">Executive Order 06-44</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt adds elementary and secondary education as another category with representation on the Regional Homeland Security Oversight Committees. (Oct. 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_045">Executive Order 06-45</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt directs the Department of Social Services to prepare a quarterly Medicaid beneficiary employer report to be known as the Missouri Health Care Responsibility Report starting in 2008. (Nov. 27)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_046">Executive Order 06-46</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe storms that began November 30, 2006.  (Dec. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_047">Executive Order 06-47</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities due to the severe weather beginning November 30, 2006.  (Dec. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_048">Executive Order 06-48</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on November 29, 2006.  (Dec. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_049">Executive Order 06-49</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt orders the Department of Mental Health to implement the recommendations of the Mental Health Task Force to make certain no instance of abuse or neglect in public or private mental health facilities is overlooked. (Dec. 19)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_050">Executive Order 06-50</a></strong><br>Gov. Matt Blunt extends the declaration of emergency contained in <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_046">Executive Order 06-46</a> and the terms of <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_048">Executive Order 06-48</a> through March 1, 2007, for clean-up in the aftermath of severe storms. (Dec. 28)</p>
</div>
<p>
